---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="About Make AI Games"
  description="Why Make AI Games exists: a transparent, data-driven map of AI game development tools for beginners and indie developers."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <div class="answer">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is a data-driven map of every AI tool for making games, built for beginners and indie developers
        who want straight answers: what each tool does, what it costs, whether you can sell what it makes, and how it
        compares.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Most "best AI game maker" articles are written by vendors ranking themselves first. We wanted one place with a
      a published scoring method, verified facts and side-by-side comparisons. We're vendors too (see our
      <a href="/disclosure">disclosure</a>), which is why the rules are public and the scores are computed rather than
      hand-picked.
    </p>
    <h2>How it stays current</h2>
    <p>
      Tool data lives in structured files. Automated agents re-check every tool weekly against its own pricing,
      changelog and status pages and propose changes with sources. Automated checks run before anything goes
      live.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
